  "t": "p",
  "c": [
   "Project-Based Learning (PBL) provides youth with authentic opportunities for leadership development and allows young people to drive their learning through inquiry, apply knowledge, and connect to what matters most to them. PBL is more than the project or product of learning at the end. It is a way of designing units that promote both authenticity and inquiry, especially now when technology has changed the way we live, work, play and learn, as stated by Junor Barnett, Director of Adult Workforce & Career Development Services and Technology Instructor."
